ModTrap: notices
================

ModTrap is our own code under the MIT licence (LICENSE).

1. Programs ModTrap calls and never contains
--------------------------------------------

- Mod Organizer 2 (GPL-3.0). ModTrap starts the owner's own installed copy from its command line and reads the
  instance's text files. No MO2 code is copied or bundled.
- xEdit / SSEEdit (MPL-2.0). ModTrap starts the owner's own installed copy, through MO2, with ModTrap's own script.
  No xEdit code or script is copied or bundled; ModTrap's script is written from scratch against xEdit's scripting
  functions.

2. Code reused from the owner's other projects
----------------------------------------------

None yet (design stage). The plan is to reuse parts of DataPiler (MIT): its local page server and its checks, its
job runner's shape, its updater and its Windows launcher. Each reused part is listed here when it lands, with the
file it came from.

3. Dependencies
---------------

None. The plan is the Python standard library only.

4. Mods
-------

No mod file, plugin or part of one is in this repository or in any release. Test fixtures are tiny plugins written
by ModTrap's own test code, with invented names and contents.
